WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.440
I stand before you today-

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.160
-to say these words.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.200
I announce my candidacy for President of the
United States of America.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.580
Nearly a dozen Democrats are already running
for president

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.840
and highlights so far include an interview
about immigration

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.640
live-streamed from a dental chair,

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.200
a former Harvard professor popping a beer
like jes’ plain folks on New Year’s Eve

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.440
and a draconian former prosecutor pledging
her allegiance to Wakanda.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.820
Payed for by Kamala Harris.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.860
Democrats are tripping over each other to
pitch Medicare for All, Free College for All,

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.720
Jobs for All, and laying taxes on wealth as
well as income.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.080
And then there’s Howard Schultz.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.300
I think the Democrats need a little bit less
caffeine right now.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.200
The former CEO of Starbucks,announced that
he is considering a run for president

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.220
as a “centrist independent.”

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:51.260
He says that the national debt threatens economic
growth,

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.900
that we shouldn’t demonize successful entrepreneurs,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.199
and that the government can’t be all things
to all people.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:04.160
Both parties are consistently not doing what's
necessary on behalf of the American people

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.160
and are engaged every single day in revenge
politics.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.660
That brought public hate, contempt, and character
assassination

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.560
from every conceivable angle.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.200
It’s not just anti-globalist lefties on
the attack.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:29.300
The New York Times op-ed page says he’s
narcissistic, delusional, and fanatical.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:34.140
His potential run, his critics claim, would
be nothing short of “reckless idiocy.”

00:01:34.149 --> 00:01:39.579
Schultz’s belief that neither major party
represents America is widely shared.

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:43.060
A plurality of Americans don’t identify
with either party.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:47.700
And nearly three-quarters of us think the
country is headed in the wrong direction,

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.880
which helps to explain why neither Hillary
Clinton nor Donald Trump

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.290
won a majority of the popular vote in 2016.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.740
The two-party duopoly and its supporters in
the media

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:59.120
understand how widely disliked they are,

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.500
which is why they want to kneecap anyone who
isn’t on Team Red or Team Blue.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.020
You don’t have to agree with Schultz

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:08.500
to understand that having more ideas and more voices at the table

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.080
at this point in the election cycle is a good
thing,

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.420
especially when you consider the alternatives.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.340
Democrats fear people such as Schultz

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.120
because they think he will drain votes whoever
their nominee ends up being,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.530
giving Trump a path to re-election.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.860
But that’s actually faulty analysis.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.000
Former Republican Congressman John Anderson

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.560
was blamed for pulling votes from Jimmy Carter
in 1980,

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:34.100
but almost half his supporters would have
gone with Ronald Reagan as their second choice.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:38.660
In 1992, the GOP fingered Ross Perot as a
political saboteur,

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:43.180
but in fact the 19 percent of Americans who
pulled the lever for the Texas Billionaire

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.160
were equally split between Bush and Clinton
as their fallback.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.040
If variety in armpit aroma isn’t his thing,

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.160
I’d like to believe that the Vermont socialist

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.360
still believes we should have more choice
at the ballot box.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.440
Right now, there are more forms of hepatitis
than viable political parties in America.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:11.140
So it’s kind of fitting that the former
CEO of a company

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.450
that introduced infinite choice in coffee
drinks

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.990
is now being dragged for threatening to expand
the political spectrum

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:19.180
all the way from A to C.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:23.720
If American politics can’t stand even the
possibility of an independent candidate

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.500
who praises capitalism, opposes massive tax
increases,

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.700
and wants to cut federal debt, we’re already
screwed in 2020.

